WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.900
Ownership.

2
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:06.333
The Federal Modernization Workbook's Book
07 Chapter 05 says an expired certificate

3
00:00:06.333 --> 00:00:11.154
is almost always an ownership failure
first, so every certificate class has

4
00:00:11.154 --> 00:00:15.975
one renewal owner, who answers for it
even when automation does the renewing.

5
00:00:15.975 --> 00:00:18.138
The platform is where that's recorded.

6
00:00:18.138 --> 00:00:21.525
What the platform provides:
placement rules and placement

7
00:00:21.525 --> 00:00:24.775
jobs move discovered certificates
into policy folders.

8
00:00:24.775 --> 00:00:28.123
A folder's policy sets
inherited configuration,

9
00:00:28.123 --> 00:00:30.550
such as the CA template and key size.

10
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:35.350
Object permissions are granted on folders
and objects, and Teams group the people.

11
00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:39.835
The documented roles are Master Admin,
Server Owner, Certificate Approver

12
00:00:39.835 --> 00:00:44.175
and Team Owner, and workflows can
require approvals at lifecycle stages.

13
00:00:44.175 --> 00:00:47.438
The program's design guidance
turns that into ownership.

14
00:00:47.438 --> 00:00:52.261
Build the policy tree to mirror Book
07 Chapter 05's certificate classes,

15
00:00:52.261 --> 00:00:56.763
so a certificate's folder tells you
its class and its renewal engine.

16
00:00:56.763 --> 00:00:59.600
Give every certificate
a named Server Owner.

17
00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.123
Map Teams to Entra groups;
release 26.1 adds SCIM 2.0,

18
00:01:04.123 --> 00:01:08.425
and CyberArk lists Entra
ID as supported for it.

19
00:01:08.425 --> 00:01:12.802
If the agency adopts the ServiceNow
app, which we'll see next, associate

20
00:01:12.802 --> 00:01:15.746
certificates with
configuration items so the

21
00:01:15.746 --> 00:01:18.312
CMDB owner and the platform's owner agree.

22
00:01:18.312 --> 00:01:23.330
And follow Chapter 08's alert: any
certificate within two renewal windows of

23
00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:28.587
expiry with no renewal path bound to it is
an incident while it can still be fixed.

24
00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:33.301
Sources: CyberArk 26.1 Placement
rules; Policies overview;

25
00:01:33.301 --> 00:01:39.487
Permissions and abilities; Teams and
policy folder permissions; Workflows;

26
00:01:39.487 --> 00:01:45.182
Configuring expiration event
intervals; Notifications and logging;

27
00:01:45.182 --> 00:01:50.386
Notification channels; What's New
(SCIM 2.0); Vendor support for SSO;

28
00:01:50.386 --> 00:01:56.420
ServiceNow Store, Machine Identity
Protection; Book 07, Chapters 05 and 08.
